    'trivy-db / fail / stale': "Content database trivy-db (trivy-repo) is stale: built <TIMESTAMP>, 4d 4h old, past its 24h bound (trivy-repo's own bound); age read from `VulnerabilityDB.UpdatedAt` in `trivy version --format json`, the database's own build time. The scan fails: a clean result from a stale database is not evidence of a clean target. To refresh it, run `trivy image --download-db-only` with network access, or copy a current trivy database into the cache directory trivy reads. To scan against it anyway, pass --allow-stale-content-db or set `content_db_staleness: warn` in the ASH config.",
